            <ArticleTitle>[Examination of the Untoward Removal of the Epidural Catheter Due to Differences in Its Fixation Methods].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>804-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Epidural anesthesia is a useful tool for postoperative pain control. However, inappropriate fixing of the catheter not only hinders the analgesic effect, but could lead to serious accidents as a result of the untoward removal of the epidural catheter.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">In our hospital, in order to reduce the removal of catheter, we introduced a new method of fixing by Steri-StripTM from fiscal 2011.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">We compared 2337 cases of epidural use for general anesthesia in one fiscal year of 2010. In fiscal year 2011, 2500 examples were examined backward.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The group using the Steri-Strip, was able to significantly reduce the untoward removal (P = 0.002).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
